# Dropdown menus & comboboxes

## Appearance

Dropdown **menus** (the panel that opens from a select / picker / menu button) are **neutral** — not brand accent.

- Panel background: `var(--editor-surface)` (or equivalent chrome surface), not `--accent` / `--accent-wb`.
- Item hover / selected: `var(--menu-item-hover)` / `var(--menu-item-active)` (or `var(--sidebar-hover)`). Do **not** use `--sidebar-active`, `rgba(var(--accent-rgb), …)`, or `color: var(--accent)` on menu items.
- Triggers may still use accent for focus / expanded border; the **menu panel and its items** stay neutral.
- Exception: destructive items may use `--danger`.

## Placement (up vs down)

Decide open direction **when building the control**, using viewport space — never hard-code `above`/`below` “for now” and leave a follow-up.

- Use `placeAnchoredMenu` from `src/lib/menuPlacement.ts` (or `placeChatComposerMenu` for chat-composer anchors).
- Default `prefer: "below"`; bottom-docked UI (chat composer) uses `prefer: "above"` via `placeChatComposerMenu`.
- Do not pass `menuPlacement="below"|"above"` on `Select` unless there is a hard layout constraint; default is `auto`.
- Recompute on open, resize, and scroll (existing Select / picker pattern).

## Checklist for a new dropdown

1. Portal + fixed position (or absolute only when the parent never clips and sits at a viewport edge).
2. `placeAnchoredMenu` / `placeChatComposerMenu` for side + `maxHeight`.
3. Neutral menu CSS — no accent fill or accent selected text.
4. Leading icons: Flat Color (`react-icons/fc`) via `menuIcons.tsx` / `treeIcons.tsx` — see `menu-icons.mdc`.
